  WDL                       https://www.cockos.com/wdl/
  Copyright (c) 2005 and later Cockos Incorporated

  Vendored as deps/wdl/verbengine.h, heapbuf.h, denormal.h and wdltypes.h.
  verbengine.h is the Reverb pedal's engine; it is in turn derived from the
  public-domain Freeverb by Jezar at Dreampoint (June 2000,
  http://www.dreampoint.co.uk), as its own header records. heapbuf.h is the
  buffer it allocates through, denormal.h flushes the denormals the Reverb's and
  the Delay's feedback paths would otherwise generate, and wdltypes.h is what
  those two include.

  WDL is Cockos' own platform-independent library. The copy vendored here was
  taken from the checkout inside iPlug2 at third_party/NeuralAmpModelerPlugin,
  because that is where a copy already sat on this machine -- but NO iPlug2 code
  is used, linked or included. iPlug2's own IPlug/Extras headers (LFO.h, SVF.h,
  DCBlocker.h, Smoothers.h) were considered and REJECTED, because each reaches
  IPlugPlatform.h or IPlugConstants.h and would drag that framework into the
  include graph. The four files above include nothing but each other and the C
  standard library, and are verified to build on Linux with -Wall -Wextra.

